(220460, 12466, 1041, '<td valign="top">Natasha, sorry I didn''t get around to voting and commenting on this one ... it''s an absolutely beautiful portrait of you and your husband.  I also like the story behind it ... probably because I''m from Germany and my husband is from the US :)</td>', 'Natasha, sorry I didn''t get around to voting and commenting on this one ... it''s an absolutely beautiful portrait of you and your husband.  I also like the story behind it ... probably because I''m from Germany and my husband is from the US :)', '2003-02-21 09:22:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(220465, 12523, 656, '<td valign="top">Congrats!  Great and fun picture</td>', 'Congrats!  Great and fun picture', '2003-02-21 09:30:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(220466, 12495, 3105, '<td valign="top">Wow!  That is a really nice shot.  Congrats.  A closer shot of the couple''s upper bodies and heads (leaving the gown to flow through the bottom of the frame) would look really nice too.  Plus that could eliminate the snow chunk.  The exposure is excellent too.<br/>Courtenay</td>', 'Wow!  That is a really nice shot.  Congrats.  A closer shot of the couple''s upper bodies and heads (leaving the gown to flow through the bottom of the frame) would look really nice too.  Plus that could eliminate the snow chunk.  The exposure is excellent too.Courtenay', '2003-02-21 09:31:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(220468, 12519, 5982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jacko:</b></div><hr/><i>Excellent one of my favorites this week.  Please give us the details of your entry.  Loved the high key effect.  Jacko.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks to you and all the other commenters!  This shot was done this way:  I was a bit at the last minute and couldn''t come with a setup so, I wore bright red lipstick and took a macro shot of my mouth.  By playing with high saturation and contrats keys I was able to remove all the skin tones leaving the background totally white.  Then I rotated the image, stretched the canvas and Voilà!  Is that digital art as someone mentioned?  I''m not sure since the image is not really distorted from it''s original state...<br/> <br/>Hope that answers your questions!  <br/> <br/>And thanks again for your great comments!<br/> <br/>Nathalie</td>', 'Originally posted by Jacko:Excellent one of my favorites this week.  Please give us the details of your entry.  Loved the high key effect.  Jacko.  Thanks to you and all the other commenters!  This shot was done this way:  I was a bit at the last minute and couldn''t come with a setup so, I wore bright red lipstick and took a macro shot of my mouth.  By playing with high saturation and contrats keys I was able to remove all the skin tones leaving the background totally white.  Then I rotated the image, stretched the canvas and Voilà!  Is that digital art as someone mentioned?  I''m not sure since the image is not really distorted from it''s original state... Hope that answers your questions!   And thanks again for your great comments! Nathalie', '2003-02-21 09:35:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(220481, 12495, 1078, '<td valign="top">Hey, I wonder exactly where THAT was taken.  ;-)  Nice shot and congrats.</td>', 'Hey, I wonder exactly where THAT was taken.  ;-)  Nice shot and congrats.', '2003-02-21 10:16:50.000000', NULL, 0),
